# gui

Vite + vanilla TypeScript + Tailwind CSS. Two screens: **Play** a match against `game-engine`, and **Replay** GNU Backgammon SGF ([ADR 0010](docs/decisions/0010-replay-player.md), [ADR 0026](docs/decisions/0026-gui-tailwind.md), [ADR 0027](docs/decisions/0027-gui-play-vs-engine.md)). The board is the `board` custom element ([ADR 0033](docs/decisions/0033-board-package.md)). Spec: [gui.md](docs/domain/gui.md).

- From `gui/`. Host commands: [README.md](README.md) (http://localhost:5173). Do not run `test:inner` / `dev` on the host. Mount `<backgammon-board>` (`import "board/element"`). No backend of its own.
- Play: human is `p1`, engine `p2`; match with live cube and Crawford; browser random dice. Talk to the engine only via `POST /api/engine/evaluate` and `POST /api/engine/cube` (Vite proxy to `ENGINE_URL`); send position JSON. Engine plays `moves[0]`; its offer and take are its own `/cube` answers (ADR 0032). Do not re-rank engine moves or add MET or cube math to the GUI.
- Play input: click a checker → first die (display order) that gives a legal step; Swap dice / Undo / Done. The element emits `point` and `swap`. Legality = prefix of `ts-core` `generateLegalSequences`. Pure rules live in `src/play/rules.ts` (tested). Set `xgid` from `positionToXgid`; the element animates the diff. `usedDice`, `movable`, and `swap` are properties.
- Replay: `FF[4]` `GM[6]` files from `move-dumper/dumps/<batch>/replay/` or `battle-arena/replays/`; file picker only, no JSONL. Previous / Next is one roll, checker step, or cube action. Rebuild position JSON by applying SGF events from the standard opening with `ts-core`, then set the element’s XGID. The match-file parser stays here.
- Do not import `move-dumper`. Do not import Node-only `ts-core` exports (`match`, `sim`, `gnubg`, `http`, `xg`, …). Do not treat SGF or play results as training data.
- Style the chrome with Tailwind utility classes. The board’s CSS lives in `board`. Minimal look: solid readable colors, no gradients, no decorative shadows. Dice and checker motion are the widget’s. Animations ignore the OS reduce-motion setting.
